	title 'TaskMaster'************************************************************************ TaskMaster (All by itself)** Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-89* All rights reserved* Original Code written by Dan Oliver* ********************************************************************************************************************************************** CHANGE HISTORY** 22 June 88	Harry Yee*	Converted to MAX development system. ** 20 Sep 88	Steven Glass** Added features to task master so that it will find and track control* and handle keystrokes.** 04 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Got TaskMasterDA working.** 06 Oct 88	Steven Glass** There are a number of places where the event record pointer can get * trashed.  I've tried to identify them all and restore it after * this occurs.** 20 Oct 88	Dan O.** Implemented TaskMaster multi-click.  Task record had to be extended.* Made CompileString a tool call.** 22 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Minor change to TaskMaster to preserve register around call to * ckDoubleClick.** 01 Dec 88	Steven Glass** Changed the way CkActiveate works so that the controls are* not drawn, but rather their rects are made invalid.** Changed TaskMasterKey to see if there is a top window before * sending events to it.** 22 Jan 89	Steven Glass** Changed routine that passed idle events on to controls.  We had* a problem that we were passing too many events including events* that were only idle because the DeskManager handled them.  We* now only pass them if the event manager says no event and the* event code is zero.*** 15 Feb 89	Dave Good** Added code to pass menu item events to the active control. I added a* new taskmaster code (wInControlMenu) which is returned as an action only* to inform the application that the control already accepted the menu* item. The way that menu events are passed to controls is a little funny;* I replace the event.what field of the task record with wInSpecial or wInMenuBar* depending on which item numbers are being passed. The menu item ID is passed* in TaskData, just as it would be returned to the application. If the control* returns non zero, I return a null task code to the application since the* control took the menu event. If the control returns zero, I pass the menu event* back to the application.** 19 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Made InvertIfNecessary into a subroutine and called it from* inside TaskMasterContent and TaskMasterKey.** Changed way SendEventToCtl is called to save code (in TaskMaster).** 20 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Removed non-TaskMaster calls (now in file NewCalls.asm).* Made TaskMaster stack-based so it would be re-entrant.** 23 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Fixed bug in update routine.  StartDrawing is now called before* user routine is called.  ZeroOrigin is called after.** 13 Mar 89	** Fixed bug in TaskMasterKey (BRC #45532, 45533). Origin was not being * set up correctly when control was being selected. ** 3/15/89	Mensch* Fixed brc #45932. Now return window ptr in task data when a control* key equiv is being used.** 28 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Changed ck_activate to call futzCtls rather than invalctls.  This* lets controls that are not going to do total redraws to optimize* their handling of activation.** 30 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Saved port around handling idle events in TaskMaster.** 31 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Pulled yesterday's change and made a global change to save* and restore grafPort.** 31 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Pushed right value for TaskMasterDA case.** 09 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Found that busyflag was always set when going into CDAs if* TaskMaster was being used.  Problem was that TaskMaster incremented* the busy flag before calling GetNextEvent (where CDA menu was* displayed).  So we moved the call.** Also took out a little redundant code that was found in the * code review we had last Tuesday.** 13 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Save DBR and D-page in global data area so it can be used by* w-def proc.** 19 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Change to code that tracks controls.  Treats scroll bars* specially.** Change to code that calls Task_menu2 in TaskMasterKey so * that handled events are returned correctly.** 8/24/89	Mensch** Implement the tmNoGetNextEvent bit in taskmask. When this bit is set* TaskMaster does not call SystemTask or GetNextEvent, the event record* MUST be already filled in by the application.* **********************************************************************	blanks off	print Push	print off	include 'all.macros'	include 'WindMgrEquates.asm'	include ':::ControlMgr:CtlCustomEqus.asm'	MACRO	bccl &A	bcs  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	beql &A	bne  @dontTake	brl  &A@dontTake	MEND	MACRO	PushWordSpace	pha	MEND	print pop************************************************************************ Equates for direct page during execution of task master***********************************************************************	DefineStackWindMgrD	wordThisAction	wordTheTaskMask	LONGWindPtr	LONGDataPtr	LONGCallingFlag	WORDOrigB	BYTEOrigD	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3InputTaskRecPtr	LONGInputEventMask	WORDOutputTaskCode	WORD	title 'TaskMaster'*****************************************************************TaskMaster	PROC EXPORT** App's little helper***   IN:    PUSH:WORD - space for result code*          PUSH:WORD - event mask used when calling GetNextEvent.*          PUSH:LONG - pointer to Task record.**  OUT:    WORD - Same as Event Code with a few changes:** External Refs:	IMPORT ckDoubleClick	import ePop6Bytes	import Task_Menu	import MakeGPIntoWP	import Do_Update2	import CkActivate	import BreakOut	import PushFrontWindow	import CallProc2** Entry Points:	ENTRY DAEntry*	longa on	; mode	longi on*** Change History** 22 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Saved task code around call to check double click.** 22 Jan 89	Steven Glass** Changed routine that passed idle events on to controls.  We had* a problem that we were passing too many events including events* that were only idle because the DeskManager handled them.  We* now only pass them if the event manager says no event and the* event code is zero.** 19 feb 89	Steven Glass** Changed way SendEvtToCtl was called to save code.** 20 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Started conversion to Stack Based code** 30 Mar 89	Steven Glass** TaskMaster now preserves the grafPort even when the idle * event is sent to the target control.** 31 Mar 89	Steven Glass** TaskMaster saves the port on entry and restores it on exit.** Change above is removed as being redundant.** 31 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Pushed right value for TaskMasterDA case.* * 13 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Save DBR and D-page in global data area for w-def proc.** 8/25/89	Mensch** Add tmNoGetNextEvent bit.* Add tmModalWindow bit.*****************************************************************	phd	Save d-page and dbr on stack	phb	tcd	Switch in wmgr's dPage for a momment	pea $0000	Push CallingFlag of zero to indicate call originDAEntry	pei <Data+2	Push pointer to window mgr's globals	pei <Data	pha	Push space for Window Pointer	pha	pha	Push space for the task mask	pha	pea $0000	ThisAction starts as zero	phd	Push window manager's direct page!	tsc	Turn our stack into direct page	tcd	pha	Save the Port on the stack	pha	_GetPort	bit CallingFlag	bpl DoNormalStuff	pei CallingFlag	; push a non-zero value so it looks like there was an event.	bra SkipNormalStuffDoNormalStuff;; Call System Task now and get it over with;; 8/24/89 Mensch; Added code here to skip getNextEvent in the case where the tmNoGetNextEvent bit is set in the; task mask.	ldy #taskMask+2	; get high word of the task mask	lda [InputTaskRecPtr],y	and #tmNoGetNextEvent	beq @getEvent	; if zero, get an event here; If we get this far, then no call to get next event should be made,; what we will do instead is get the taskwhat field and push it on the stack as the result of ; getnextevent, so that we can proceed	lda [InputTaskRecPtr] ; event what is first field	pha	bra SkipNormalStuff	  ; and continue with the rest of the call...@getEvent;	_SystemTask		Call Desk Manager so it can pass a tick.	pha	pei InputEventMask	pei InputTaskRecPtr+2	pei InputTaskRecPtr	_GetNextEventSkipNormalStuff	jsl IncBusyFlg		Inc flag so that shared resources are in danger;; Put d-page and dbr in global data for use by w-def Procs.; 13 Apr 89 SEG	ldy #callerDPage	lda OrigD	sta [<dataPtr],y	ldy #callerDataB		high byte must be valid	lda OrigB-1	sta [<DataPtr],y; End Change	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr]	Check this so we don't zero important data	cmp #wInContent		for TaskMasterDA case	beq SkipThisShit		ldy #message		Clone message into TaskData just in case.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	ldy #TaskData+2	sta [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	dey	dey	txa	sta [<InputTaskRecPtr],ySkipThisShit	ldy #TaskMask+2		Get TaskMask into a	zero page location.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	sta TheTaskMask+2	and #$FF80		Bits 23-31 must be clear.	beq mask_ok	pla		Get rid of return flag from GetNextEvent.	stz OutputTaskCode		Return event state.	ldy #TaskMaskErr	 	Bits 21-31 not clear in TaskMask err.	brl UnlinkWithErrormask_ok	dey	dey	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	sta <TheTaskMask	pla		Get returned flag from GetNextEvent.	bne do_event;-----------------------------------------------------------;; If we get here, then the event was null or taken by the ; desk manager.  If it was really null, see if we ; should send it on to the active control;	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr]	bne NotNull	lda TheTaskMask+2	and #tmIdleEvents	beq NotNull	pha	; is there a window?	pha	_FrontWindow	lda 3,s	ora 1,s	bne ThereIsAWindowNoWindow	pla	; no window, clean the stack	pla	bra NotNullThereIsAWindow	_StartDrawing	; start drawing in front window so can send idle	pha	; space for result	PushWord #True	; Send only to active control	lda #0	; zero means front window	pha	pha	pei InputTaskRecPtr+2	pei InputTaskRecPtr	_SendEventToCtl	pla	; ignore result	lda #0	; reset origin	pha	pha	_SetOriginNotNull;-----------------------------------------------------------	ldx #inNull	No event to act on if MenuSelect off.	jsr task_menu	brl GoHome	Return event flag.;;; --- Event happened, handle it ----------------------------;; --- Is this an event the Task Master should handle? ------;do_event	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr]	Event code.	cmp #inButtDwn	Button down event?	beq ck_butt	cmp #inKey	Key event?	beq ck_key	cmp #inAutoKey	Auto key?	beq ck_key	cmp #inActWind	Activate/Inactivate	event?	beq ck_act	cmp #inUpdate	Update event?	beq ck_update; not an event we will handle.	tax	put code in x-reg	brl GoHome	and clear out.ck_update	tax	Save inUpdate.	lda <TheTaskMask	Ok to handle update	event?	and #TM_UPDATE	bne ok31	brl GoHome	Update feature is masked off.;ok31	jsr MakeGPIntoWP	turn TaskData into a pointer to wind record;	jsr do_update2	Have application draw update region.;	tax	Was update handled?	bne skip3	lda #inUpdate	Tell caller that update was performed.	sta <ThisAction;skip3	brl GoHome;;;; --- Never fear, Task Master will handle the event. ------------------------;; ------- Check to redraw controls for activate/inactivate events -----------;; Always return the inActWind event code in case application wants to ; do more with the event.; ck_act	pha	Save event code.	jsr ckactivate	Redraw window's controls.	plx	Get inActWind event	code.	brl GoHome	Return event code to user.;;; ------- Call routine to handle keys ------------------;ck_key	pha	pha	pei <InputTaskRecPtr+2	pei <InputTaskRecPtr	jsr PushFrontWindow	_TaskMasterKey	brl JoinTMContent;;; ------- Handle button down event -------------------------------;ck_butt		pha	Save the event code	lda <InputTaskRecPtr	Pass pointer to task record.	ldx <InputTaskRecPtr+2	jsr ckDoubleClick	Set double-click fields.	plx	Get event code off stack	lda <TheTaskMask	Ok to handle button	down event?	and #TM_FINDW	bne ok32	brl GoHome	Button handler is masked off.;; Call FindWindow;ok32	pha		Return space.	ldx <InputTaskRecPtr+2	Return window pointer in TaskData.	lda <InputTaskRecPtr	clc	adc #TaskData	bcc store1	inxstore1	phx	pha	ldy #where+2		Pass point where button down.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	pha		Find if down on window.	_FindWindow	plx		Get returned value.;; At this point, check to see if the tmModalWindow bit is set and if it is call the modal window; routine...	lda <theTaskMask+2	; get the taskmask	and #tmModalWindow	; test the modal window bit	beq @NoModalWindow	; if zero, we are not using modal windows	cpx #$0013	; is it an inContent? if not then its an error	bne @NotInModal	; and we should simply report it.	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	; get the front most window (it would be the modal one)	pla	; get the result into <X> and <A>	plx	ldy #taskData	; now compare the result from findwindow	cmp [InputTaskRecPtr],y	bne @NotInModal	iny	iny	txa	cmp [InputTaskRecPtr],y	beq @InModalWindow	; if both are equal we are in a modal window and we should continue; This routine will be called if we are not inside of a modal window@NotInModal	ldx #wNotInModal	; return the not in modal result	brl goHome	; and exit the call...;;@InModalWindow	ldx #$0013	; reload the inContent message and continue@NoModalWindow;; ------- Handle system menu bar interaction ----------------------;	cpx #wInMenuBar	bne next5;	stx <ThisAction	Assume this will be the action (its changed if it is different)	jsr task_menu	Handle system menu bar.	brl GoHome	x = return code.;;; --- Do some common setups --------------------------------------;next5	jsr breakout	Break out parameters from event rec.	bit CallingFlag	bpl @CheckForSystem	txa	and #$7FFF	bra ok6@CheckForSystem	txa	Get value returned from FindWindow.	bpl ok6	System window?;;; --- Handle system	window ---------------------------------------;	lda <TheTaskMask	Ok to handle system	window event?	and #TM_SYSCLK	bne ok35	brl GoHome	System window feature is masked off.;ok35	pei <InputTaskRecPtr+2	Pass pointer to event record.	pei <InputTaskRecPtr	pei <WindPtr+2	Pass pointer to window's port.	pei <WindPtr	phx	Pass result from FindWindow.	_SystemClick;	lda #wClickCalled	SystemClick called.	sta <ThisAction;null_out	ldx #0	bra GoHome;;; --- Handle the specific task -----------------------------------;ok6	ldy #taskRequest	Save task code.	sta [<DataPtr],y	ldx WindMgrD	sta >work,x	Pass result from FindWindow to callProc2.;	sec	sbc #$0013	bcs ok8	lda #6	Can't handle if because out of range.ok8	asl a	tax	lda >masks,x	beq dontHandle	bpl ok10	and <TheTaskMask	beq ok9;dontHandle	ldy #taskRequest	Get task code.	lda [<DataPtr],y	bra ckControls;ok10	and <TheTaskMask	beq dontHandle;ok9		jsr MakeGPIntoWP		turn TaskData into a pointer to wind record	phd		Save our local D-page; Put the windPtr (the real one) on window managers; direct page.	ldx WindMgrD	lda WindPtr			sta >Wind,x	lda WindPtr+2	sta >Wind+2,x	ldx <InputTaskRecPtr	Pass pointer to task record.	ldy <InputTaskRecPtr+2	lda #wTask		Pass command.	pei WindMgrD		Make WindMgr D-Page current	pld	jsr callProc2	pld		Restore our local D-page;	                  		a = result, x = action taken.;ckControls	cmp #wInContent	bne skip7	pha	pha	pei <InputTaskRecPtr+2	pei <InputTaskRecPtr	_TaskMasterContentjoinTMContent	plx	; action take	pla	; result codeskip7	stx <ThisAction	tax	; --- Return to caller --------------------------------------------;; X-reg contains the value to be put in OutputTaskCode and; ThisAction contains the value of the taskCode acted on if; OutputTaskCode is zero.;GoHome	stx OutputTaskCode		Return result to caller	txa		Null event?	bne UnlinkWithoutError	lda <ThisAction	ldy #TaskData		Return action performed in TaskData.	sta [<InputTaskRecPtr],y;UnLinkWithoutError	ldy #0		Indicate No ErrorUnLinkWithError	sty WindMgrD		Save error  for momment	_SetPort		restore port from stack	ldy WindMgrD		Get error back	pla		Pull off WindMgrs D	pla		Pull off ThisAction	pla		Pull Off TaskMask	pla	pla		Pull Off window pointer	pla	pla		Pull Off window manager globals	pla	pla		Pull off Calling Flag; dbr already on stack!	brl epop6bytes;;masks	DC.W TM_CONTENT	$0013     0 wInContent	DC.W TM_DRAGW	$0014     1 wInDrag	DC.W TM_GROW	$0015     2 wInGrow	DC.W TM_CLOSE	$0016     3 wInGoAway	DC.W TM_ZOOM	$0017     4 wInZoom	DC.W TM_INFO	$0018     5 wInInfo	DC.W 0	$0019     6 wInSpecial	DC.W 0	$001A     7 wInDeskItem	DC.W TM_SCROLL	$001B     8 wInDeskItem;	ENDP	title 'TaskMasterContent'*****************************************************************TaskMasterContent   PROC EXPORT** Description*** Inputs:*	none*	taskData = window to track controls in.** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	import InvertIfNecessary** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*** Change History** 19 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Treat scroll bars specially so that after tracking the control, * we always return the part code of the scroll bar.** The problem arrised if you tracked the scroll for a while and* then pulled out.  The app might think nothing happend.** Worksheet # BCOJHS111*****************************************************************	DefineStackTMsD	wordMyTemp	longRet1	block 3Ret2	block 3Event	longResult	long	pha	pha	phd	tsc	tcd;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Assume that there are no controls.;	lda #wInContent	sta Result+2	stz Result;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Look and see if program wants me to look for controls;	ldy #NewTaskRecord.TaskMask+2	lda [<event],y	and #tmContentControls	bne LookForControls	brl CleanStack;;; --- Only look for controls in top window.;LookForControls	pha	Space for result.	pha	_FrontWindow	pla	plx	ldy #taskData	cmp [<event],y	bne @exit	txa	iny	iny	cmp [<event],y	beq @ok1@exit	brl CleanStack@ok1;-----------------------------------------------------------;; The program wants me to look for controls, so I start; by zeroing out the output fields in the task record.;; Zero taskData2, taskData3 and taskData4;;	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskData2	lda #0Loop	sta [<event],y	iny	iny	cpy #NewTaskRecord.taskData2+12	bcc Loop;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Before trying to find the control, fix the window ; coordinate system.;	jsr PushWPtr	_StartDrawing;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Call find control;	pha	lda <event		Pointer to TaskData2	clc	adc #NewTaskRecord.taskData2	tax	lda <event+2	adc #0	pha	phx	ldy #where+2		Pass point where button down.	lda [<event],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<event],y	pha		Find if down on window.	jsr PushWPtr	_FindControl	pla	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskData3	sta [<event],y	tay		Was anything found?	bne FoundAControl	brl NoControlFoundFoundAControl;-----------------------------------------------------------;; put ControlID into taskData4;	pha	Get control ID	pha	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskData2+2	lda [<event],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<event],y	pha	_GetCtlID	pla	plx	bcs NoID	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskData4	sta [<event],y	iny	iny	txa	sta [<event],yNoID;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Track the control;	pha	ldy #where+2	Pass point where button down.	lda [<event],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<event],y	pha	Find if down on window.	pea $FFFF	pea $FFFF	jsr PushTaskData2	_TrackControl;; was this a scroll bar (but not the thumb);	ldy #newTaskRecord.TaskData3	lda [<event],y	cmp #upArrow	bcc NotScroll	cmp #pageDown+1	bcs NotScroll	pla	bra YesScrollNotScroll	pla	beq GaveUpYesScroll	ldy #newTaskRecord.TaskData3+2	sta [<event],y;-----------------------------------------------------------;; If the type is a check control or a radio control, ; then we have to diddle with its value.;	jsr PushTaskData2	pla	plx		jsr InvertIfNecessary	lda #wInControl	ldx #0	bra GetOutNoControlFound	lda #wInContent	ldx #0	bra GetOutGaveUp	lda #0	ldx #wInContentGetOut	sta Result+2	stx Result	lda #0	pha	pha	_SetOriginCleanStack	lda Ret1+4	; move the rtl address up 4 bytes	sta Ret1+4+4	lda Ret1+2	sta Ret1+2+4	lda Ret1	sta Ret1+4	pld	; restore d-reg	pla	; clean off 4 bytes of temp storage	pla	pla	; clean off 4bytes of input	pla	lda #0	; return no error	clc	rtlPushWPtr	plx	ldy #NewTaskRecord.TaskData+2	bra JoinPusherPushTaskData2	plx	ldy #NewTaskRecord.TaskData2+2JoinPusher	lda [<event],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<event],y	pha	phx	rts	ENDP	title 'TaskMasterKey'*****************************************************************TaskMasterKey	PROC EXPORT** This is the routine that handles keystrokes.  We've broken* it out from the rest of task master so that it will be * easy to patch (if necessary).*** Inputs:*     Space For result         LONG*     Pointer To TaskRec       LONG*     Pointer To Front Window  LONG** Outputs:*     HiWord  Function Result for TaskMaster*     LoWORD  Original Event we handled*	** External Refs:	import task_menu2	import InvertIfNecessary** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*** Change History** 01 Dec 88	Steven Glass** Checked to see if there was a top window before calling trying* to send keystrokes to it.** 08 Feb 89	Harry Yee** If DATaskFlag is negative, then we were called by TaskMasterDA otherwise* we were just called by TaskMaster. If we were called by TaskMasterDA then* then the top window must be a system window otherwise the key event is* not passed on. If we were called by TaskMaster then the top window cannot* be a system window otherwise the key event will not get passed on.*** 15 Feb 89	Dave Good** The last change didn't work; harry gave me some new code and I implemented* it. Key events should be passed to the controls properly now.** 19 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Called invertIfNeccessary if inControl is returned for keystrokes.** 20 Feb 89	Steven Glass** If the original calling program is TaskMasterDA, then we do* not send the keystroke to MenuKey.** 13 Mar 89	Steven Glass and Harry Yee** The origin was being set to zero before InvertIfNecessary was called.* This would cause controls to be drawn incorrectly. BRC #45532, 45533.** 19 Apr 89	Steven Glass and Harry Yee** TaskMaster could not return wClosedNDA, wCalledSysEdit, wInControlMenu* or wInDeskItem.  This was caused by TaskMenu2's return of the action* taken being ignored here.  So now we look at it if the action is taken.*****************************************************************	DefineStackTMsD	wordRet1	block 3Ret2	block 3TheTopWind	longEvent	longResult	long	phd	tsc	tcd;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Start by copy the event to result.;	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskWhat	lda [event],y	sta Result	sta Result+2;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Now see if the key is a menu key.;TryMenus	ldx TMsD	lda >CallingFlag,x	bne CannotBeMenuKey	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskmask	lda [event],y	and #TM_MENUKEY	beq TryCtlKey;ok30	pei <event+2	Pass pointer to event.	pei <event	lda #0	Pass pointer to menu bar,	pha	zero = system menu bar.	pha	_MenuKey	phd	Switch TaskMasters D back in and call...	lda TMsD	tcd	ldx #inKey	Just in case its not a menu	stx <ThisAction	Init this field too	jsr task_menu2	lda <ThisAction	pld	restore my d-page	stx Result+2	cpx #inKey	beq TryCtlKey	keep trying	sta Result	bra GetOutCannotBeMenuKeyTryCtlKey;-----------------------------------------------------------;; See if the user wants to send key to controls.;	ldy #4	;four bytes into the window is a flag that tells us whether	lda [<TheTopWind],y	;..this is a system or application window	ldx TMsD	eor >CallingFlag,x	;..window and TaskMaster then pass key, otherwise exit	and #$8000	;if system window and TaskDA then pass key. If application	beq @WeMatch	brl GetOut@WeMatch	lda >TheTaskMask+2,x	and #TMcontrolKey	beq GetOut;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Zero taskData2, taskData3 and taskData4;	ldy #NewTaskRecord.taskData2	lda #0Loop	sta [<event],y	iny	iny	cpy #NewTaskRecord.taskData2+12	bcc Loop;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Lets see if there even is a window;	lda TheTopWind	ora TheTopWind+2	beq GetOut;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Before doing anything else, fix the window ; coordinate system.;	pei TheTopWind+2	pei TheTopWind	_StartDrawing;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Now we send the key to the controls;	pha	PushWord #False	pei TheTopWind+2	pei TheTopWind	pei event+2	pei event	_SendEventToCtl;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Look at the result;	pla	beq ZeroAndGetOut	lda #wInControl	sta Result+2;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Added 3/15/89	Mensch; Return the front window pointer in taskData because a control in; that window was just messed with.	ldy #TaskData	; offset to taskdata in the event record	lda <TheTopWind	; place the top window pointer into task data	sta [<event],y	ldy #TaskData+2	lda <TheTopWind+2	sta [<event],y; End of change	ldy #NewTaskRecord.TaskData2+2	lda [event],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [event],y	jsr InvertIfNecessaryZeroAndGetOut;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Fix the origin	lda #0	pha	pha	_SetOriginGetOut	lda Ret1+4	; move the rtl address up 4 bytes	sta Ret1+4+8	lda Ret1+2	sta Ret1+2+8	lda Ret1	sta Ret1+8	pld	; restore d-reg	pla	; clean off 8 bytes of input	pla	pla	pla	lda #0	; return no error	clc	rtl	endp	title 'TaskMasterDA'*****************************************************************TaskMasterDA	PROC EXPORT** This is the routine that can be called by desk accessories* that to let TaskMaster do its work for it.*** Inputs:*     Space For result         WORD*     DummyWord	           WORD*     Pointer To TaskRec       LONG** Outputs:*     WORD    ResultCode (same as task master*	** External Refs:*	import task_menu2** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	phd	Save d-page and dbr on stack	phb	tcd	Switch in wmgr's dPage for a momment	pea $FFFF	Push CallingFlag of -1 to indicate call origin	brl DAEntry	endp	title 'BreakOut'*****************************************************************breakout	PROC** Gets window pointer from event record and puts it into WindPtr.*** Inputs:*	InputTaskRecPtr** Outputs:*	WindPtr** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	ldy #TaskData	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	sta <WindPtr	iny	iny	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	sta <WindPtr+2	rts	ENDP	title 'do_update2'*****************************************************************do_update2	PROC** Have the application draw the update region*** Inputs:*	WindPtr is pointer to window's grafPort*	OrigD ** Outputs:*	a-reg:  0 if update was handled*	        wInUpdate if not handled** External Refs:	import LongCall	import ZeroOrigin** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 23 Feb 89	Steven Glass** In original implementation of this routine, shared* direct page made it possible to call internal window manager* routines rather than the making real calls.** The stack based re-write made us make real calls including**     BeginUpdate*     StartDrawing*     ZeroOrigin*     EndUpdate******************************************************************	ldx #inUpdate	ldy #wContDraw	Is there an address	of a redraw routine?	lda [<WindPtr],y	iny	ora [<WindPtr],y	beq exit;	jsr PushWinPtr	_BeginUpdate	jsr PushWinPtr	_StartDrawing;	ldy #wContDraw+1	Get address of draw	routine.	lda [<WindPtr],y	tax	dey	lda [<WindPtr],y;	phd	Save my zero page.	phb	Save current data bank.;	pei OrigB-1	plb	plb	pei OrigD	pld	jsl longCall;	plb	Restore last data bank.	pld	Switch to my zero page.;	jsr ZeroOrigin	jsr PushWinPtr	_EndUpdate;	ldx #0	Null event, event handled flag.;exit	txa	Return event flag in A.	rtsPushWinPtr	plx	ldy #TaskData+2	lda [InputTaskRecPtr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [InputTaskRecPtr],y	pha	phx	rts	ENDP	title 'task_menu'*****************************************************************task_menu	PROC** Handles system menu bar interactions for TaskMaster.*** Inputs:*	x-reg   wInMenuBar** Outputs:*	x-reg   Task master return code** External Refs:	import PushFrontWindow** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda <TheTaskMask		Ok to call MenuSelect?	and #TM_MENUSLT	bne ok1exit1	rts		MenuSelect handler is masked off.;ok1	pei <InputTaskRecPtr+2	Pass pointer to event record.	pei <InputTaskRecPtr	lda #0		System menu bar flag.	pha	pha	_MenuSelect		Let user make a selection.;	ldx #Null		Just in case.;;	ENTRY task_menu2task_menu2     ;	ldy #TaskData		See if there was a selection.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	bne selection;	lda <TheTaskMask		Allow selection of inactive menu items?	and #TM_INACTIVE	beq exit1;	iny	iny	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	Inactive item selected?	beq exit1;	ldx #wInactMenu		Inactive item selected event.	rts		No selection made.;; --- Handle special menu selection -----------------------------------------;selection	ldx #wInMenuBar		Application menu selection made.;	cmp #256		Special or desk accessory item ID?	bcs doCtrlMenu		IDs greater than 255 are application's.;	cmp #250		Special or Desk accessory item ID?	bccl desk_item;;; ------ Special Undo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Clear, Close item ------------------;	lda <TheTaskMask	and #TM_SPECIAL		Ok to handle it?	beq skip4;	pha	jsr PushFrontWindow	_GetSysWFlag	pla	beqL doCtrlSpecial		Application window if positive.;;; -------------- Handle special item for system window -----------------------;	ldy #TaskData		See if there was a selection.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	cmp #255		Close command?	bne edit_item;;; -----------------	Close item select with system window on	top --------------;	jsr PushFrontWindow	_CloseNDAbyWinPtr		Close desk accessory window.;	lda #wClosedNDA		Tell user that desk	accessory was closed.	brl unliteMenu;;; -----------------	Edit item selected with system window on top -------------;edit_item	pha		Space for result.	sec	sbc #249		Proper command edit	command.	pha	_SystemEdit	lda #wCalledSysEdit		Action, just in case.	plx	bne unliteMenu		Did Desk Manager handle it?;skip4	ldx #wInSpecial		Special menu item.	rts;---------------------------------------------------------------;; See if the controls want to know about menu selections;doCtrlMenu	ldy  #NewTaskRecord.TaskMask+2	lda  [InputTaskRecPtr],y	and  #tmControlMenu	beq  @exit2	phx		;save the correct menu event to return	lda  [<InputTaskRecPtr]	;save the event.what field	pha	txa		;pass the correct menu event to the	sta  [<InputTaskRecPtr]	;..control	PushWordSpace		;space for result	PushWord #True		;only send menu events to the active ctrl	PushLong #0		;use the front window	pei InputTaskRecPtr+2	pei InputTaskRecPtr	_SendEventToCtl	pla	beq  @exit1	pla		;restore the event.what field	sta  [<InputTaskRecPtr]	pla		;cleanup the stack	lda  #wInControlMenu	bra  unliteMenu@exit1	pla		;restore the event.what field	sta  [<InputTaskRecPtr]	plx		;get back the correct menu event@exit2	rtsdoCtrlSpecial	ldx  #wInSpecial		;use the wInSpecial event	bra  doCtrlMenu;; --- Desk accessory menu item ---------------------------;desk_item		ldx #wInDeskItem		Desk accessory event, just in case.;	lda <TheTaskMask		Ok to handle desk accessory event?	and #TM_OPENNDA	beq exit2		Let application handle desk accessory.;	pha		Space for result.	ldy #TaskData	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	pha		Pass item ID number.	_OpenNDA		Open desk accessory.	pla		Throw away returned	ref value.;	lda #wInDeskItem		Tell application that a desk accessory;			was opened.	unliteMenu	sta <ThisAction;	pea 0		Unhighlight.	ldy #TaskData+2	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	Pass selected menu's ID,	pha		to HiliteMenu.	_HiliteMenu;	ldx #Null		Menu selection was handled.exit2	rts		x = task return code.	ENDP	title 'PushFrontWindow'*****************************************************************PushFrontWindow	PROC** Returns the pointer to the window's grafPort.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	window's grafPort ptr on stack** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	plx	pha	pha	phx	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	pla	plx	sta 3,s	txa	sta 5,s	rts	ENDP	title 'ckActivate'*****************************************************************ckactivate	PROC** Check to handle activate/inactivate events.** WindPtr is trashed.*** Inputs:*	TheTaskMask*	InputTaskRecPtr** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	import MakeGPIntoWP** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 01 Dec 88	Steven Glass** If the window is active and the control tie bit is clear, * then we invalidate the controls (we used to draw the controls).* Drawing the controls made them draw twice (once for activate* and once for the update).  Now the only draw during the update.*****************************************************************;;	lda <TheTaskMask	Check if it's ok to try and handle	and #TM_CREDRAW	the event.	beq exit	If not, just exit.;	jsr MakeGPIntoWP	turn TaskData into a pointer to wind record;	ldy #wframe	Check if controls are tied to window's	lda [<WindPtr],y	activate state.	and #F_CTL_TIE	bne exit	If not, just exit.;	jsr breakout	Get window port pointer.;	ldy #NewTaskRecord.TaskModifiers	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	and #$0001		; only care about low bit	pha	pei WindPtr+2	pei WindPtr;	_FutzCtls	ldx #$3610	jsl $E10000exit	rts	ENDP	title 'MakeGPIntoWP'*****************************************************************MakeGPIntoWP	PROC** This routine takes the window's grafPort pointer in* taskData and turns it into a window record pointer* putting the result in WindPtr*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	WindPtr** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	stz <WindPtr	stz <WindPtr+2	ldy #TaskData+2	Break out pointer to window effected.	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	dey	dey	tax	beq IsZero	lda [<InputTaskRecPtr],y	sec	sbc #wport	sta <WindPtr	bcs NoBorrow	dexNoBorrow	stx <WindPtr+2IsZero	rts	ENDP	title 'InvertIfNecessary'*****************************************************************InvertIfNecessary	PROC** This routine takes a control handle as input in a & x and* checks to see if the control is a checkbox or radio button* control.  If it is such a control, we change the* control value.*** Inputs:*	a & x = control handle** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 19 Feb 89	STeven Glass** This used to be in line code inside Taskmaster Content.* It is now a subroutine so that it can be called from* inside TaskMasterKey.*****************************************************************	DefineStackCallersD	wordTempA	longTempB	longRTS	word	phx	pha	phx	pha	phd	tsc	tcd		lda [TempA]		deref handle	tax	ldy #2	lda [TempA],y	sta TempB+2	stx TempB	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc	Look at the Proc ref	lda [TempB],y	bne NotSpecial		If not zero, its not check or radio	iny	iny	lda [TempB],y	and #$7FFF	cmp #^checkControl**$7FFFFFFF	Is it check?	bne NotCheck	pha		Get Current Check value	pei TempA+2	pei TempA	_GetCtlValue	pla	beq SetValueTo1	PushWord #0	bra SetTheValueNotCheck	cmp #^radioControl**$7FFFFFFF	Is it radio	bne NotSpecialSetValueTo1	PushWord #1SetTheValue	pei TempA+2	pei TempA	_SetCtlValueNotSpecial	pld	pla	pla	pla	pla	rts	ENDP	title 'ckDoubleClick'*****************************************************************ckDoubleClick	PROC EXPORT** Set the appropriate double click fields in the taskrecord.***   IN:	x/a = pointer to task record.*	Called only when there has been a button down.*	ClickCount field must be set to zero by *	    application first time record is used.**  Out:             All registers trashed.** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************;@saveDpage	equ 1@taskRec	equ @saveDpage+2;;	phx	Save pointer to task record.	pha;	phd	Save caller's direct page pointer.	tsc	Switch direct page into stack.	tcd;;; --- Check if caller wants double-clicks checked.;	ldy #taskMask+2	lda [<@taskRec],y	and #tmMultiClick	beq @exit;	ldy #clickCount	Is this the first time through?	lda [<@taskRec],y	beq @singleClick	Set first click.;;; --- Check for multi click.;	ldy #when	lda [<@taskRec],y	Time of this click.	sec	ldy #lastClickWhen	sbc [<@taskRec],y	less time of last click,	tax	ldy #when+2	lda [<@taskRec],y	ldy #lastClickWhen+2	sbc [<@taskRec],y	equals time inbetween.	bne @singleClick	Is it a double click?;	phx	Save time between clicks.	pha	Space for result.	pha	_GetDblTime	pla	plx	cmp 1,s	Is double-click speed less than the	pla	time between clicks?	bcc @singleClick	If it is, no multi click, reset to single.;	ldy #lastClicky	Is position of new click near last?	lda [<@taskRec],y	sec	ldy #where+y1	sbc [<@taskRec],y	clc	adc #2	cmp #7	bcs @singleClick;	ldy #lastClickx	lda [<@taskRec],y	sec	ldy #where+x1	sbc [<@taskRec],y	clc	adc #3	cmp #11	bcs @singleClick;	ldy #clickCount	Multi click, increment number of clicks.	lda [<@taskRec],y	inc a	bra @storeClick;;; --- Set information about this click in task record.;@singleClick	lda #1	Set click number.	ldy #clickCount@storeClick	sta [<@taskRec],y	ldy #when	Set when.	ldx #lastClickWhen+2	jsr @moveLong	ldy #where	Set where.	ldx #lastClicky+2	jsr @moveLong;;; --- Clean up stack and exit.;@exit	pld	Restore caller's direct page pointer.	plx	clean up stack (removing pointer pushed at	plx	beginning).	rts;--------------------------------------------;	Move a long within task record.;--------------------------------------------;;   IN: y = source index.;       x = destination index + 2.;@moveLong	lda [<@taskRec],y	pha	iny	iny	lda [<@taskRec],y	txy	sta [<@taskRec],y	dey	dey	pla	sta [<@taskRec],y	rts	ENDP	END